course: dictionary
lesson: 2506
title: Decapods: animals with ten legs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A decapod is a crustacean with ten legs, such as a crab, lobster, shrimp, prawn or crayfish. Look at the word in parts: deca means ten, and pod means foot. That is a clue to the meaning, and it also matches the ten legs.
explain: Decapods belong to the crustaceans, and crustaceans belong to the arthropods. Arthropods are animals with jointed legs and a hard outer skeleton. So a decapod is a kind of crustacean, and a crustacean is a kind of arthropod: each word is a group inside the bigger one.
explain: «A woodlouse has 14 legs and is a crustacean, related to crabs; a crab has ten legs counting its claws, which is why it is called a decapod.» Two of the ten legs are often big claws, called pincers. A woodlouse is not a decapod, because it has more than ten legs.
fact: A decapod is a crustacean with ten legs.
fact: Crabs, lobsters, shrimps, prawns and crayfish are all decapods.
fact: Decapods are crustaceans, and crustaceans are arthropods: animals with jointed legs and a hard outer skeleton.
fact: Two of a decapod's ten legs are often big claws, called pincers.
fact: «Decapod» comes from Greek words meaning ten and foot.
exercise: What is a decapod? | A plant with ten leaves | A bird with two wings | A fish with no bones | *A crustacean with ten legs
exercise: Which of these animals is a decapod? | Spider | Snail | *Lobster | Butterfly
exercise: Decapods are crustaceans. Crustaceans belong to which bigger group? | Mammals | Molluscs | *Arthropods | Flowering plants
test: Two of a decapod's ten legs are often big claws. What are they called? | Antennae | *Pincers | Wings | Fins
test: How many legs does a decapod have? | *Ten | Fourteen | Six | Eight
exam: Which of these is NOT a decapod? | Lobster | Crayfish | Prawn | *Woodlouse
